    '/images/destinations/gujarat/hero.jpg',
    $$Gujarat is a land of luminous contrasts, where boundless desert wilderness meets centuries of mercantile wealth and imperial craftsmanship. Along the northern frontier lies the Great Rann of Kutch - the world's largest seasonal salt desert. Stretching toward the horizon in a blinding expanse of pure white salt crystals, this surreal landscape reflects the sky like a giant mirror. Under the light of a full moon, the Rann turns into a dreamscape of shimmering silver, home to semi-nomadic artisan communities whose vibrant hand-embroideries bring brilliant color to the barren earth.$$,
