(
    'kashmir',
    'Kashmir & The Vale of Srinagar',
    'Himalayas & Ladakh',
    $$Mughal Garden Terraces, Cedar Houseboats & Alpine Splendor$$,
    '/images/destinations/kashmir/hero.jpg',
    $$Framed by the snow-crowned amphitheatre of the Pir Panjal and Great Himalayan ranges, the Vale of Kashmir has been celebrated for centuries as heaven on earth (*Firdaus bar roo-ye zameen*). At the heart of this high-altitude basin lies Srinagar, a city organized around the aquatic poetry of Dal and Nigeen Lakes. Here, morning mist rises from still waters like spun silk, revealing hundreds of intricately carved cedar-wood houseboats, their Victorian fretwork reflected in mirror-smooth water lilies.$$,
    $$March to May (Spring Blossom & Tulip Radiance - prime touring climate)$$,
    $$10°C - 22°C$$,
    $$6 to 9 Days$$,
    $$["Dawn Private Cedar Shikara to the Floating Dawn Market: Private morning navigation aboard a luxury cedar shikara across mist-covered Dal Lake to the 200-year-old floa...","Curator-Led Architectural Walk of Shalimar & Nishat Mughal Gardens: Private after-hours exploration of the Mughal pleasure gardens with an architectural historian, examining the ...","Hangul Deer Tracking Expedition in Dachigam National Park: Exclusive morning wildlife safari in Dachigam National Park with a senior wildlife biologist, tracking the cri...","Master Atelier Visit: Authentic Kani & Sozni Pashmina Guilds: Behind-the-scenes access to a multigenerational family karkhana (workshop) in the Old City of Srinagar, observ...","Helicopter Flight & Gondola Ascent to Apharwat Peak, Gulmarg: Private helicopter transfer to Gulmarg, followed by VIP skip-the-line boarding on the Gulmarg Gondola to Aphar..."]$$::jsonb,
    $$["/images/destinations/kashmir/hero.jpg","/images/destinations/kashmir/dal-lake-shikara.jpg","/images/destinations/kashmir/mughal-gardens.jpg","/images/destinations/kashmir/gulmarg-himalayas.jpg"]$$::jsonb,
