  ),
(
    'central-india',
    'Central India & Khajuraho Heritage Corridor',
    'Central India',
    $$Medieval Dynastic Temples, River Cenotaphs & Sovereign Tiger Forests$$,
    '/images/destinations/central-india/hero.jpg',
    $$The Central Indian heritage corridor encompasses a majestic cross-section of Indian antiquity. Stretching from the sandstone temple hills of Khajuraho across the medieval fortresses of Orchha to the dense sal forests of Bandhavgarh and Kanha, this is a realm where the boundary between human artistry and primeval nature dissolves entirely.$$,
    $$October to March (Golden Winter - prime touring climate)$$,
    $$10°C - 26°C Day / 4°C - 10°C Night$$,
    $$6 to 9 Days$$,
    $$["Private Sunrise Architectural Tour of the Western Group of Khajuraho: Private, early morning access to the Kandariya Mahadeva and Lakshmana temples with a senior archaeological sch...","Twilight Flute & Sitar Salon at the Orchha Cenotaphs on the River Betwa: Private candlelit reception on the banks of the Betwa River directly facing the illuminated Bundela cenotaphs,...","Private Core-Zone Tiger Tracking in Bandhavgarh with Master Naturalists: Full-day private safari permit across the Tala and Magdhi core zones in an open 4x4 safari vehicle, tracking t...","Dawn Barasingha Safari across Kanha's Maiden Grasslands: Morning game drive across the mist-covered central meadows of Kanha, observing the rare hard-ground barasingha...","Private River Safari on the Ken River Canyon, Panna: Boat expedition through the deep sandstone gorges of the Ken River inside Panna Tiger Reserve, observing nesti..."]$$::jsonb,
    $$["/images/destinations/central-india/hero.jpg","/images/destinations/central-india/khajuraho-temple.jpg","/images/destinations/central-india/orchha-cenotaphs.jpg","/images/destinations/central-india/bandhavgarh-tiger.jpg"]$$::jsonb,
    true
  ),
(
    'tamil-nadu',
    'Tamil Nadu & The Great Living Chola Temples',
    'South India',
    $$Imperial Granite Vimanas, Merchant Palaces & Sacred Classical Arts$$,
    '/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/hero.jpg',
    $$Tamil Nadu is the guardian of unbroken Dravidian civilization. Unlike northern realms whose architectural monuments were repeatedly reshaped by successive waves of conquest, the Cauvery Delta and southern plains of Tamil Nadu have preserved their classical language, ritual temple architecture, and philosophical traditions for more than two millennia. This is an empire of monumental granite, where soaring temple towers (*gopurams*) encrusted with thousands of painted deities dominate the palm-fringed horizon.$$,
    $$November to February (Golden Winter - prime touring climate)$$,
    $$20°C - 30°C$$,
    $$7 to 10 Days$$,
    $$["Private Pre-Dawn VIP Darshan at Brihadisvara Temple, Thanjavur: Curator-led private dawn access to the inner corridors and courtyards of the Great Chola Temple before public ...","Private Twilight Temple Procession at Madurai Meenakshi Temple: Exclusive VIP entry to witness the sacred night procession (*palliyarai*) at the Meenakshi Amman Temple, as th...","Architectural Exploration of Private Chettinad Mansions: Private walking tour of Kanadukathan and Kottaiyur led by a Chettinad heritage conservationist, gaining exclus...","Master Lost-Wax Bronze Casting Masterclass in Swamimalai: Private workshop visit to a 10th-generation master sthapathi family in Swamimalai, observing the creation of b...","Private Chamber Carnatic Veena or Vocal Recital: Intimate evening chamber concert inside the central courtyard of Visalam or Svatma, featuring renowned classic..."]$$::jsonb,
    $$["/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/hero.jpg","/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/thanjavur-temple.jpg","/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/madurai-meenakshi.jpg","/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/chettinad-mansion.jpg","/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/mahabalipuram-shore-temple.jpg","/images/destinations/tamil-nadu/hotel-the-leela-chennai.jpg"]$$::jsonb,
    true
  ),
(
    'hampi',
    'Hampi & The Vijayanagara Imperial Ruins',
    'South India',
    $$Monolithic Granite Ruins, Mythic Boulders & Forgotten Empires$$,
    '/images/destinations/hampi/hero.jpg',
    $$Hampi exists in an otherworldly realm where human architectural ambition meets primeval geological fantasy. Spread across 4,000 hectares of rugged terrain in north-central Karnataka, the landscape is defined by millions of giant, rust-colored granite boulders precariously balanced across arid hillsides, bisected by the emerald currents of the sacred Tungabhadra River.$$,
    $$November to February (Golden Winter - prime touring climate)$$,
    $$16°C - 30°C$$,
    $$4 to 6 Days$$,
    $$["Private Coracle River Glide along the Tungabhadra at Dawn: Private sunrise excursion in a traditional wicker coracle boat across the quiet currents of the Tungabhadra, f...","Curator-Led Architectural Exploration of the Vittala Temple: Exclusive pre-opening access to the Vittala Temple complex with an epigraphist and architectural historian, ex...","Private Sunset Champagne Reception atop Malyavanta Hill: Private evening ascent to Malyavanta Raghunatha Temple or Hemakuta Hill, sipping chilled champagne on the warm...","Curated Expedition to the 6th-Century Rock Caves of Badami & Pattadakal: Private full-day excursion in a luxury SUV to the red sandstone cave temples of Badami and the UNESCO temples ...","Private Corbelled Bathing & Royal Court Dinner at Evolve Back: Multi-course imperial court dinner hosted on the private terrace of Kamalapura Palace, featuring royal Vijayan..."]$$::jsonb,
    $$["/images/destinations/hampi/hero.jpg","/images/destinations/hampi/virupaksha-temple.jpg","/images/destinations/hampi/tungabhadra-river.jpg","/images/destinations/hampi/hotel-evolve-back.jpg"]$$::jsonb,
    true
  ),
(
    'gujarat',
    'The White Desert & Royal Kingdoms of Gujarat',
    'Western India',
    $$White Salt Expanses, Asiatic Lions & Imperial Solanki Heritage$$,
    '/images/destinations/gujarat/hero.jpg',
    $$Gujarat is a land of luminous contrasts, where boundless desert wilderness meets centuries of mercantile wealth and imperial craftsmanship. Along the northern frontier lies the Great Rann of Kutch - the world's largest seasonal salt desert. Stretching toward the horizon in a blinding expanse of pure white salt crystals, this surreal landscape reflects the sky like a giant mirror. Under the light of a full moon, the Rann turns into a dreamscape of shimmering silver, home to semi-nomadic artisan communities whose vibrant hand-embroideries bring brilliant color to the barren earth.$$,
    $$October to March (Golden Winter / Salt Desert Season - prime touring climate)$$,
    $$12°C - 28°C Day / 8°C - 14°C Night$$,
    $$7 to 10 Days$$,
    $$["Full-Moon Midnight Excursion on the Great Rann of Kutch: Private evening expedition into the silent, white salt flats under the radiance of the full moon, accompanied ...","Private Open-Top 4x4 Asiatic Lion Safari in Gir National Park: Exclusive morning and evening game drives in Gir's core wildlife tracking zone led by a senior naturalist and ...","Masterclass with the Master of Rogan Art in Nirona: Private studio session in Nirona village with the Khatri family, observing the transformation of boiled castor...","Curator Salon at the Patan Patola Double-Ikat Silk Loom: Exclusive visit to the private home-museum of the Salvi master weavers in Patan, witnessing the mathematical d...","Private Dawn Exploration of Rani ki Vav & Modhera Sun Temple: Curator-led private dawn visit to the UNESCO stepwell of Rani ki Vav and the Modhera Sun Temple before public ..."]$$::jsonb,
    $$["/images/destinations/gujarat/hero.jpg","/images/destinations/gujarat/modhera-sun-temple.jpg","/images/destinations/gujarat/gir-asiatic-lion.jpg","/images/destinations/gujarat/rani-ki-vav.jpg","/images/destinations/gujarat/hotel-aramness-gir.jpg","/images/destinations/gujarat/hotel-rann-luxury-camp.jpg"]$$::jsonb,
    true
  ),
(
