    $$Mughal Garden Terraces, Cedar Houseboats & Alpine Splendor$$,
    '/images/destinations/kashmir/hero.jpg',
    $$Framed by the snow-crowned amphitheatre of the Pir Panjal and Great Himalayan ranges, the Vale of Kashmir has been celebrated for centuries as heaven on earth (*Firdaus bar roo-ye zameen*). At the heart of this high-altitude basin lies Srinagar, a city organized around the aquatic poetry of Dal and Nigeen Lakes. Here, morning mist rises from still waters like spun silk, revealing hundreds of intricately carved cedar-wood houseboats, their Victorian fretwork reflected in mirror-smooth water lilies.$$,
