    '/images/destinations/sikkim-darjeeling/hero.jpg',
    $$The Eastern Himalayas of Darjeeling and Sikkim rise in steep, mist-shrouded green terraces toward the third highest mountain on earth: Mount Kanchenjunga (8,586 m). Here, where Tibetan Buddhism meets British colonial hill-station heritage, the air is scented with woodsmoke, mountain pine, and the fragrant, floral aroma of freshly plucked tea leaves.$$,
